[{:db/id "82e1672b-a1cf-5e4f-b7ec-400e71ee5eb2" :answer/id #uuid "82e1672b-a1cf-5e4f-b7ec-400e71ee5eb2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{37}$ and $\\frac{2\\sqrt{73}}{3}$" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b3598dd1-c765-5f19-9a18-ce18efdacfdc" :answer/id #uuid "b3598dd1-c765-5f19-9a18-ce18efdacfdc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{37}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{3}$" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d4ab06df-aa62-554d-b1a3-91a2d87f977e" :answer/id #uuid "d4ab06df-aa62-554d-b1a3-91a2d87f977e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{37}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{3}$" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "cb386ed9-a60a-507f-a0a0-3b956d0d46eb" :answer/id #uuid "cb386ed9-a60a-507f-a0a0-3b956d0d46eb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{37}$ and $\\frac{2\\sqrt{73}}{3}$" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6e7a2f97-cecf-54f4-977c-ad480185865c" :answer/id #uuid "6e7a2f97-cecf-54f4-977c-ad480185865c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$37$ and $\\frac{73}{9}$" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "db39f157-86de-5b5e-aa65-9e3ecfdb909d" :answer-field/id #uuid "db39f157-86de-5b5e-aa65-9e3ecfdb909d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["82e1672b-a1cf-5e4f-b7ec-400e71ee5eb2" "b3598dd1-c765-5f19-9a18-ce18efdacfdc" "d4ab06df-aa62-554d-b1a3-91a2d87f977e" "cb386ed9-a60a-507f-a0a0-3b956d0d46eb" "6e7a2f97-cecf-54f4-977c-ad480185865c"] :answer-field/correct "82e1672b-a1cf-5e4f-b7ec-400e71ee5eb2" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "a8e4213c-472e-5df6-a92b-8b65321f34cc" :question/id #uuid "a8e4213c-472e-5df6-a92b-8b65321f34cc" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{37}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\frac{73}{9}}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=37$ and ${b}^{2}=\\frac{73}{9}.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=37,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{37}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=\\frac{73}{9},$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{\\frac{73}{9}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{3}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=\\sqrt{37},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{37}=2\\sqrt{37},$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{3}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{73}}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["db39f157-86de-5b5e-aa65-9e3ecfdb909d"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "ce4db2e6-57cc-53c9-a74c-1ffe1f592efd" :answer/id #uuid "ce4db2e6-57cc-53c9-a74c-1ffe1f592efd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{70}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9736611d-7a2c-5da0-acc9-2bf3c1d58488" :answer-field/id #uuid "9736611d-7a2c-5da0-acc9-2bf3c1d58488" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["ce4db2e6-57cc-53c9-a74c-1ffe1f592efd"] :answer-field/correct "ce4db2e6-57cc-53c9-a74c-1ffe1f592efd" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "bbc2dfdf-cb86-5fc6-aae5-463332bc08d9" :answer/id #uuid "bbc2dfdf-cb86-5fc6-aae5-463332bc08d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{82}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c6df07a4-3e4e-56fb-903b-6dca2e87c255" :answer-field/id #uuid "c6df07a4-3e4e-56fb-903b-6dca2e87c255" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["bbc2dfdf-cb86-5fc6-aae5-463332bc08d9"] :answer-field/correct "bbc2dfdf-cb86-5fc6-aae5-463332bc08d9" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "3a6ef55b-f35c-5e25-8e8b-c766bf7961eb" :question/id #uuid "3a6ef55b-f35c-5e25-8e8b-c766bf7961eb" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\frac{82}{9}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{70}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=\\frac{82}{9}$ and ${b}^{2}=70.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=\\frac{82}{9},$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{\\frac{82}{9}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{82}}{3}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=70,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{70}.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $b=\\sqrt{70},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\frac{\\sqrt{82}}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{70}=2\\sqrt{70},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{82}}{3}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{82}}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["9736611d-7a2c-5da0-acc9-2bf3c1d58488" "c6df07a4-3e4e-56fb-903b-6dca2e87c255"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "6418b296-10d2-5b35-b945-05b31aba2d9e" :answer/id #uuid "6418b296-10d2-5b35-b945-05b31aba2d9e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{17}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}$" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d502494b-1775-539d-9e06-67be767210e8" :answer/id #uuid "d502494b-1775-539d-9e06-67be767210e8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{17}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}$" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d3bb7b1f-836e-5b98-9cdd-890c7f95b0ea" :answer/id #uuid "d3bb7b1f-836e-5b98-9cdd-890c7f95b0ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{17}$ and $\\sqrt{13}$" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "90328bb5-2efb-5b62-9495-b0a760fef10a" :answer/id #uuid "90328bb5-2efb-5b62-9495-b0a760fef10a" :a